### Login as restaurant 2
POST http://localhost:3001/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "restaurantId": 2,
  "password": "taco123"
}

###

### Check session after logging in as restaurant 2
GET http://localhost:3001/api/auth/session

###

### Try to update restaurant 1's menu item while logged in as restaurant 2
### This should return 404 and should not update the item
PUT http://localhost:3001/api/menu-items/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Hacked Menu Item",
  "price": 1,
  "description": "Restaurant 2 should not be able to update this"
}

###

### Get restaurant 1
GET http://localhost:3001/api/restaurants/1

###

### Try to delete restaurant 1's menu item while logged in as restaurant 2
### This should return 404 and should not delete the item
DELETE http://localhost:3001/api/menu-items/1

###

### Get restaurant 1
GET http://localhost:3001/api/restaurants/1

###

### Create a menu item for restaurant 2
POST http://localhost:3001/api/menu-items
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Fish Tacos",
  "price": 12.99,
  "description": "Three fish tacos with slaw and lime crema"
}

###

### Logout restaurant 2
POST http://localhost:3001/api/auth/logout

###

### Try to create a menu item while logged out
### This should return 401
POST http://localhost:3001/api/menu-items
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Unauthorized Item",
  "price": 9.99,
  "description": "This should not be created"
}

###

### Try to update a menu item while logged out
### This should return 401
PUT http://localhost:3001/api/menu-items/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Unauthorized Update",
  "price": 9.99,
  "description": "This should not work"
}

###

### Try to delete a menu item while logged out
### This should return 401
DELETE http://localhost:3001/api/menu-items/1
